sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 52/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The tunnel (concentric rings) and spiral pullbacks in the PNG and GIF are convincing analogues of Klüver's tunnel and spiral families and of Bressloff et al.'s Fig. 31b/33b inverse maps, the four columns are visually distinct, and the cobweb pullback is a recognisable lattice of crossing log-spiral arcs. -10: nothing from a subject report or from Bressloff Fig. 1 / Ermentrout-Cowan 1979 is placed beside the output; the only reference is the paper's own model figures named in titles, and even those are not shown. -10: the honeycomb pullback is a lattice of isolated spots, not the hexagonal cells of Klüver's honeycomb or Fig. 35. -8: the GIF (the asset embedded in both READMEs) forces noncontoured mode with wave_count = 3.5, so frames 3/4 and 4/4 show four lobes and three blobs that no one would call a cobweb or a honeycomb. -6: the spiral panel has a visible seam along theta = +-pi because the wavevector's azimuthal component is not quantised to integer cycles over 2 pi beta/eps. -6: the funnel (radial rays) member of the tunnel/funnel family is never rendered and the cobweb column's retinal title reads \"mode=spiral\". -8: contoured planforms are drawn as a scalar max-over-orientation field rather than the oriented line segments the papers use, so the cobweb/honeycomb textures only loosely resemble the published double-map figures. Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): rings and spiral pullbacks recognisable; honeycomb pullback is a dot lattice; cobweb retinal title says mode=spiral; seam at theta=pi on left of spiral disc — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, image/png, 908688 B, 1972×1576 px, artifact_sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514 (sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): frames 3/4 and 4/4 show four lobes / three blobs, not cobweb or honeycomb; spiral frame has a horizontal seam — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, image/gif, 1498952 B, 640×340 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 df4acc7ae32e7ef54dcf2f78e982ae47357d3edbef3027a4a13b66d0bcecb018 (sha256 df4acc7ae32e7ef54dcf2f78e982ae47357d3edbef3027a4a13b66d0bcecb018), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1227–L1230: GIF overrides contour_mode=noncontoured, wave_count=3.5, sharpness=1.6 away from the paper presets <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1227-L1230>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L729–L742: contoured field is max-|val| over 16 orientation samples, not an oriented-segment double map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L729-L742>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.52"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphological realism / specimen match' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> .
    <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965> dct:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A mathematical theory of visual hallucination patterns" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769> dct:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "Geometric visual hallucinations, Euclidean symmetry and the functional architecture of striate cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861> dct:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "What geometric visual hallucinations tell us about the visual cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> dct:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A model for the origin and properties of flicker-induced geometric phosphenes" .
}

